gured out some of  the  pretty significant barriers of what that  would have presented to us  and and started scoping it back it  probably would have  been a really cool game but i'm not sure  it would have had the outreach  that we had uh given the move we made it  probably would have stayed through  person which would have changed the  aiming mechanics the  uh the overall feel of the uh the design  um of the game in general um all of  those core mechanics would have  really been dramatically different and  so it's it's hard to imagine  what it really could have turned into  could you imagine the uh  the next imac would just be this giant  green  uh helmet like thing with an orange  screen and a visor over it and  to protect from the sunshine outside and  yeah i  probably would have there would have  been weird things like that i'm sure  i mean we did get tons of halo themed  xboxes so it's not  that far-fetched to assume that maybe  apple would do  a themed imac i mean who knows apple did  release  a video game console back in 1996 which  was  an utter disaster but maybe they would  have released another one  hopefully not called the pip apple tv  would have had a halo tv show apple  arcade would have likely launched with a  halo ios game and most recently apple  put a ban on microsoft's  xcloud like their game streaming thing  in this case  we probably would have been streaming  halo to our phones that is even if  xcloud  would have existed what would have xbox  been like in this alternate reality  we what would xbox live be like what  would first person shooters be like  without this  [Music]  now imagining all this is arbitrary  i know but i do think there's value in  at least entertaining the what-if  scenarios of things  that could have been halo has had a  staggering  impact on the culture of games and the  identity of many gamers  what would a world have been like if we  didn't have that video of a bunch of  atlas and boys coming together  to sing a soundtrack in a bathroom  [Music]  that's a world i don't want to live in  and even still it did eventually come to  mac os  and pc and even returned to its roots as  rts  with halo wars now will halo  revolutionize games  again that timeline has yet to be  written  but one thing's for sure is that its  legacy and what's done to games  is surely set in stone  if you've made it this far thank you  very much  for watching this episode of remember  when i hope you enjoyed it now if you're  new here thanks for coming by  as well we have a bunch of episodes that  we've done some on consoles  one on resident evil another on street  fighter and the link to that and the  playlist will be in the description  below so yeah um i'm kurt and davina by  the  way  pleasure to meet you if we haven't  already been acquainted and um  that's really about it hope you're doing  well be well stay safe  okay all right see you later

